# Rust build output and the ACL/schema files tauri-build regenerates on every
# compile. Cargo.lock is NOT here on purpose: this crate produces a binary, and
# a shipped installer should be reproducible from the tree it was built from.
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# The allow/deny permissions tauri-build writes for each command the app
# declares. Same class as gen/ above: generated on every compile, stamped
# "DO NOT EDIT", and derived entirely from the list in build.rs — which is
# itself conditional, so committing these would leave files describing commands
# a default build does not have.
src-tauri/permissions/autogenerated/

# The UI bundle. Built by `npm run ui:build`; never committed, never published —
# the mirror carries the source that produces it.
dist/
# The served host-client bundle (`npm run ui:build:host`) — the third artifact, packaged as the
# app's `host-client` resource. Same rule: built output, never committed.
dist-host/
